Reproduced. The root cause is the `window.ADGMAD` and `adSkip` globals are missing.

https://github.com/AdguardTeam/AdguardFilters/blob/4aa4729ec4587d14846c26e8ec7fb26923bd6afc/JapaneseFilter/sections/specific.txt#L1656

I've designed new rule that calls the reward callback directly and override some methods to empty Promise:

```js
["outGame", "outGameSub", "inGame", "instead"]
	.forEach(function (k) {
		var s = m[k];
		if (s && typeof s.show === "function" && s.show.name !== "adgSkip") {
			s.show = function adgSkip(cb) {
				if (typeof cb === "function") {
					try {
						cb()
					}
				} return true
			}
		}
	});
if (m.imaAd) {
	m.imaAd.load = () => Promise.resolve()
	m.imaAd.show = () => Promise.resolve()
}
```

<details><summary>Tested screenshots: The rewards get directly on my end. </summary>
<img width="400" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/cef9eca3-bed3-4f53-b3ec-31e6fd12455a" />
<img width="400" alt="Image" src="https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/efc76565-ff6d-497b-a57b-b37d68f3b28a" />
</details> 

I didn't tested the rest websites yet.

